  a composed influence is scaled by the factor at its depth; past depth 4 it carries a direction and **no magnitude** — the path is still named, graded and dated, because a direction a reader cannot locate in the graph is not a direction
  several paths out of one shock share ancestry, so summing them double-counts. They are still never summed: a component with at least one path inside the attenuation boundary carries a `joint` figure combined by noisy-OR, with the dependence carried structurally — dependence is structural rather than fitted — a shared edge is drawn once per trial, so paths agree exactly to the extent that they share edges. Assumed: conditional on the shared edges the disjoint remainders are independent. Not modelled: a common cause the graph does not contain, so this corrects the double-counting the graph can see and claims nothing about the rest
